        ^"Fiery Soultaker" DEF {
            ^"Description" STRING "A wanyūdō is an Otherworldly, Tainted being of silhouette 2. When making an Attack action check, the wanyūdō may spend (op) (op) to inflict the Burning condition on its target. Characters who perish while at range 0 of a wanyūdō have their souls dragged to Jigoku. The ramifications of this terrible outcome are at the GM's discretions, such as that they cannot be reincarnated until they are rescued."
        }

        RULES {
            #L5RSH09sT9uV1wX3yZ5aB7cD: wanyudo "A wanyūdō has the bizarre form of the flaming wheel of an oxcart, with a screaming human head for its hub. It rolls with preternatural speed across virtually any terrain, including water, attempting to wrench the soul from any mortal being it encounters. Each is said to be the tortured ghost of someone who was an oppressive tyrant while alive. It is a terrifying foe, especially when encountered outside of the Shadowlands."
        }
    }

